          "source_text_sha256": "68805dca8cc26244119b793cc709997510a1be39d9066a6780f4a85853433af2",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On October 10, 1991, around 9:30 PM, numerous witnesses across all departments in southwestern France observed for a few seconds a very bright white light moving very quickly with a significant trail in a generally indicated north-south direction. Some witnesses also heard a loud explosion accompanying the phenomenon. A local newspaper article allowed many witnesses to come forward. The characteristics of the observation favor the hypothesis of a large-scale atmospheric reentry, probably natural given the observed direction.",
